    "hash": "UTdxng9jYV2+l1TT19wzZ0LRz9g=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:23:01.330Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## When to use\nTheme a Powerhouse editor or drive-app UI correctly in light and dark. Covers the bai token system ([data-bai-theme] + --bai-* vars + ThemeProvider, for vault-style packages) and design-system semantic tokens (--foreground/--background/--primary + .dark, for packages built on document-engineering, e.g. the invoice demo) plus theming third-party widgets (Select, DatePicker) whose dark: variants never generate in a consumer build, and native widgets (date/select/checkbox) via color-scheme/accent-color. Read before building or restyling any editor UI.\n\n## What it covers\n- Two systems \u2014 pick the one that matches the package\n- System A: the bai token system\n- System B: design-system semantic tokens\n- Third-party widget theming \u2014 the invoice lesson\n- Native browser widgets\n- Verification checklist\n\n## Where the full skill lives\n- Vault source: **Agent skill: theme-styling** (full text, DERIVED_FROM below) \u2014 the vault is this skill's home.\n\n## Invocation\nRead the vault source content and follow it. Not a plugin command.\n\n_Added via add-skill; content hash sha256:36dd98f74250\u2026_",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-16T20:23:01.330Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-16T20:23:01.330Z"
    }
  },
